# bridge_config — single per-CLI env file for `bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli`.
#
# WHAT IT IS
# ----------
# Consolidated env file for the withdraw-e2e CLI. Carries every parameter
# the CLI itself reads via clap `env` attrs (see
# `bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli/src/args.rs`), and nothing else.
#
# Unlike `shellnet.common` + `L{1,2}_config/env` (which target the bundle
# daemon and its deploy state), `bridge_config` targets ONLY the CLI. It
# does not source `shellnet.common` and deliberately omits daemon-only
# settings — no `BRIDGE_BOOTSTRAP_SEQNO`, `BRIDGE_ANCHOR_LEVEL`, or
# `BRIDGE_BK_SET_CONFIG`. Those belong in `L{1,2}_config/env` on the
# host running `daemon-live` (which may be a different machine from the
# CLI operator).
#
# WHAT IT DELIBERATELY OMITS
# --------------------------
# `RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY` is NOT set here. Every operator brings their own
# Sepolia EVM key. Export it in your shell (or a personal, git-ignored
# env file) before invoking the CLI:
#
#   export RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…
#
# See §"Wallet setup and bridge config" in
#   bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli/docs/live_cli_withdraw_runbook.md
# for wallet creation + Sepolia funding via the pk910 PoW or Google
# Cloud Web3 faucets. Never reuse a wallet that holds real funds; never
# commit the private key.
#
# HOW TO CONSUME
# --------------
#   cd crates/an-bridge-prover
#   export RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…            # your own key
#   set -a && source bridge_config && set +a
#   ./target/release/bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli withdraw ...
#
# Relative paths below are anchored to the working directory
# `crates/an-bridge-prover/` (same convention as `shellnet.common`).

# --- Ethereum side (Sepolia) --------------------------------------------------
RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com

# --- Acki Nacki side (shellnet) -----------------------------------------------
BRIDGE_GQL_ENDPOINT=https://shellnet.ackinacki.org/graphql

# --- local dirs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `params/` holds ~17 GB of SRS + per-circuit vk/pk files. Do NOT wipe —
# keygen would re-burn ~7 min per circuit.
BRIDGE_PARAMS_DIR=./params

# Optional — pk cache dir passed through to the C4 aggregator subprocess.
# The CLI defaults it to `$BRIDGE_PARAMS_DIR/pk_cache` if unset.
# BRIDGE_PK_CACHE_DIR=./params/pk_cache

# Optional — where per-withdrawal idempotency state files live. Defaults
# to `./withdraw-state` (relative to cwd) when unset.
# BRIDGE_WITHDRAW_STATE_DIR=./withdraw-state

# --- SHPLONK aggregation (mandatory) ------------------------------------------
# The on-chain AckiNackiBridge verifier only accepts aggregated calldata.
# The CLI refuses to submit without both dirs resolving.
BRIDGE_AGGREGATOR_DIR=../bridge-evm-aggregator
BRIDGE_VERIFIERS_DIR=../../contracts/ethereum/verifiers

# --- Deploy-dependent — REPLACE BEFORE FIRST RUN ------------------------------
# Path (a) — shared shellnet reference deploy:
#   Paste the current `AckiNackiBridge` address shared by the shellnet
#   team. Expected to stabilize once the team's Sepolia deploy is pinned;
#   until then, ask.
#
# Path (b) — you deployed your own bridge with
#   `scripts/deploy_bridge_bundle.sh` (see
#   ../bridge-relayer-daemon/docs/live_relayer_bridge_verifyBlock_runbook.md):
#   copy the `BRIDGE_ADDRESS` line from the generated `L{1,2}_config/env`.
#
# Leave commented out to force the CLI to fail loudly ("missing required
# argument BRIDGE_ADDRESS") instead of silently connecting to the wrong
# bridge.
# BRIDGE_ADDRESS=0x…
